  "77": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "**Model:** Anima (anima_baseV10.safetensors). Trained on Danbooru tags, natural language captions, and tag+caption combinations.\n\n**Tag format:** Use lowercase with spaces (not underscores). Score tags are the only tags using underscores.\n\n**Recommended positive prefix:** masterpiece, best quality, score_7, safe, \n**Recommended negative:** worst quality, low quality, score_1, score_2, score_3, artist name\n\n**Tag order:** [quality/meta/year/safety tags] [1girl/1boy/etc] [character] [series] [artist] [general tags]\n\n**Quality tags (use either or both):** masterpiece, best quality, good quality, normal quality, low quality, worst quality — and/or — score_9 through score_1.\n\n**Time period:** year 2025, year 2024, ..., newest, recent, mid, early, old\n**Meta:** highres, absurdres, anime screenshot, jpeg artifacts, official art\n**Safety:** safe, sensitive, nsfw, explicit\n\n**Artists:** Prefix with @ (e.g. @big chungus). Required — effect is weak without @.\n\n**Prompt weighting** works but needs higher weight than typical SDXL (e.g. (chibi:2)).\n\n**Full example:** year 2025, newest, normal quality, score_5, highres, safe, 1girl, oomuro sakurako, yuru yuri, @nnn yryr, smile, brown hair, hat, solo, long hair, open mouth, looking at viewer, white background, simple background\n\n**Image With Text:** Anima is able to generate image with decent qualitied text with prompts like 'holding sign above head with red painted text \"Hello!\"'\n\n**Hires fix (two-pass):** Pass 1 renders at Width×Height (~1 MP). The result is pixel-upscaled (lanczos) to UpscaleWidth×UpscaleHeight (~2 MP), re-encoded to latent space, and pass 2 re-samples at low Denoise2 to restore detail. Keep Denoise2 in 0.3–0.45 (higher drifts toward a redraw); Seed2 should differ from Seed1; keep sampler/scheduler identical across passes. Default upscale 1184×1728 matches the 832×1216 base aspect ratio — adjust both together."
    },
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "[NOTE]"
    }
  },
